WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.536
Today’s lesson goal: Today’s lesson goal: pack steps into named functions. Pass inputs with parameters. Return results you can reuse.

2
00:00:11.386 --> 00:00:22.690
What a function is: A function is a reusable recipe with a clear name. Call it whenever you need that work done. It keeps programs shorter and easier to test.

3
00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:35.276
Parameters and return: Parameters are inputs the function receives. Return sends a value back to the caller. Prefer return over only printing when you need the result later.

4
00:00:36.126 --> 00:00:50.118
Worked example: greeting: Worked example: define greet with a name parameter. Return a friendly string. Call it with different names. Reuse one function instead of copying print lines.

5
00:00:50.968 --> 00:01:04.816
Scope in plain words: Scope in plain words: names inside a function are local by default. Pass what you need in. Return what you need out. Avoid relying on hidden global variables.

6
00:01:05.666 --> 00:01:18.050
Common mistakes: Common mistakes: forgetting parentheses when calling. Forgetting return and wondering why you get None. Functions that try to do five unrelated jobs.

7
00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:31.572
Practice checkpoint: Practice checkpoint: write one function that calculates a total. Call it twice with different inputs. Then continue in the written Module 4 lesson and quiz.
